      {
        "thread_id": "TH2",
        "thread_goal": "Draft and refine the standard loading, unloading, and packing process.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M18",
            "speaker_id": 297341,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, I've created the first drafts for the Standard Loading SOP (A1) and the Packing Guidelines (A2). Please review and provide feedback. The goal is to get these solid for the pilot. This covers T2 and T3.",
            "mentions": [
              18459,
              38045,
              59367,
              66233,
              265520
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1",
              "A2",
              "T2",
              "T3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "page_facing_up",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M19",
            "speaker_id": 18459,
            "reply_to": "M18",
            "text": "In A1, section 3, it says 'distribute weight evenly'. What does that mean? Like, chemically?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M20",
            "speaker_id": 38045,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "It means not putting all the heavy stuff on one side of the vehicle. You balance it side-to-side and front-to-back to keep the truck stable.",
            "mentions": [
              18459
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "👍",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M21",
            "speaker_id": 38045,
            "reply_to": "M18",
            "text": "The docs look like a good start. For A2, under 'Bulky Items', we should add a specific point about using moving blankets and corner protectors for furniture. We have them, but people forget to use them.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M22",
            "speaker_id": 59367,
            "reply_to": "M18",
            "text": "Maybe we can design a new kind of box for fragile things. Something with better aerodynamics.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M23",
            "speaker_id": 297341,
            "reply_to": "M22",
            "text": "Let's stick to standard materials for now to stay within budget, but that's an interesting thought for the future. @38045 good point on the blankets, I'll add that in.",
            "mentions": [
              38045,
              59367
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M24",
            "speaker_id": 66233,
            "reply_to": "M18",
            "text": "In A2, for fragile items, we should specify 'double-boxing' for anything glass. Also, for items marked as chemical products, they must be packed in sealed plastic bags inside the box to prevent leaks. This is a standard practice in chemical handling.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "lightbulb",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M25",
            "speaker_id": 297341,
            "reply_to": "M24",
            "text": "Excellent points, @66233. Very important. I'll incorporate those. So, for packing rules on fragile and bulky items, we're agreeing on:\n1. Mandatory moving blankets and corner protectors for furniture.\n2. Double-boxing for all glass items.\n3. Internal sealed bags for all chemical products.\nIs everyone aligned on these rules?",
            "mentions": [
              66233
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D4"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M26",
            "speaker_id": 38045,
            "reply_to": "M25",
            "text": "Yes, that's clear and practical.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M27",
            "speaker_id": 66233,
            "reply_to": "M25",
            "text": "Yes, that covers the critical points.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M28",
            "speaker_id": 297341,
            "reply_to": "M27",
            "text": "Great, D4 is confirmed. Now for the core loading steps in A1. Based on the draft, the key steps are: 1. Pre-load vehicle check. 2. Load heavy items first, distributed evenly. 3. Build stable tiers. 4. Secure load with straps. 5. Final safety check. This is also reflected in the draft for A7. Any concerns with this flow?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1",
