      {
        "thread_id": "TH4",
        "thread_goal": "Agree on special handling steps for animals and sensitive cargo.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 265520,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hello all. As part of T5, I have drafted the Animal and Sensitive Cargo Handling Guide (A5). The key principles are ensuring proper ventilation, minimizing time in the depot, and using designated, quiet areas for staging. Please review and share your thoughts.",
            "mentions": [
              18459,
              38045,
              59367,
              66233,
              297341
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T5",
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "paw_prints",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M45",
            "speaker_id": 38045,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "This is really helpful. What's the procedure if an animal appears to be in distress during transit?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M46",
            "speaker_id": 265520,
            "reply_to": "M45",
            "text": "Good question. The guide includes an emergency contact list for veterinary services. The immediate steps are to pull over safely, check ventilation, provide water if possible, and call the number for guidance. Never open a crate on the roadside.",
            "mentions": [
              38045
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "👍",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M47",
            "speaker_id": 18459,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "Does this guide cover all animal species? What about insects or lab animals? Their needs are very different.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M48",
            "speaker_id": 265520,
            "reply_to": "M47",
            "text": "The current guide focuses on domestic pets (cats, dogs) and small livestock, which make up 99% of our animal cargo. For highly specialized transports like lab animals, the shipper must provide their own detailed protocol which we would then follow. I've added a note to clarify that.",
            "mentions": [
              18459
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M49",
            "speaker_id": 66233,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "This is well-structured. In the depot, what is a safe distance to keep animal crates from areas where we might have chemical goods or loud noises from machinery?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M50",
            "speaker_id": 265520,
            "reply_to": "M49",
            "text": "Excellent point. I'll add a requirement for a minimum 10-meter separation from any chemical storage and away from main forklift routes. The designated staging area for animals in the new depot layout should reflect this.",
            "mentions": [
              66233
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M51",
            "speaker_id": 297341,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "The guide is clear and actionable. The checklist for vehicle prep (water access, non-slip flooring, ventilation check) is particularly useful.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M52",
            "speaker_id": 265520,
            "reply_to": "M50",
            "text": "Based on the feedback, I've refined the guide. The mandatory steps are: 1. Use designated, quiet staging areas. 2. Ensure 10m separation from chemicals/noise. 3. Verify shipper paperwork and animal wellness before loading. 4. Follow vehicle prep checklist. 5. Adhere to the in-transit distress protocol. Shall we approve these as the core requirements?",
            "mentions": [
              18459,
              38045,
              59367,
              66233,
              297341
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D6"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M53",
            "speaker_id": 297341,
            "reply_to": "M52",
            "text": "This is comprehensive and covers all the safety bases. I approve.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
